%description:
Tests the new search after mtuProbeInterval (2 s here) of the path MTU search
(mtuProbing = 2), as Linux tcp_mtu_check_reprobe() and RFC 4821 section 7.2.
The scenario is that of tcp_mtu_probe_2, with 300000 bytes at t=1 and 100000
bytes at t=3.5. The path drops each packet larger than 1100 bytes, so the search
converges in the first burst, at 1.055 s, between 1098 and 1104 (less than 8
bytes apart), and it stays so for the rest of the burst. At 3.515 s, more than
mtuProbeInterval after the start of the search, the search runs again from the
MTU in use (1098) up to the MTU of the MSS of the peer (1500), and the probe of
MTU 1299 goes out (B334).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 10s
*.srv_app.sendScript="1.0 300000; 3.5 100000"
*.srv_tcp.mss = 600
*.cli_tcp.mss = 1460
*.*_tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.srv_tcp.mtuProbing = 2
*.srv_tcp.baseMss = 512
*.srv_tcp.pathMtu = 1500
*.tcptester.pathMtu = 1100
*.srv_tcp.mtuProbeInterval = 2s

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: the MTU probe of 1105 is lost, the search runs from 1098 to 1104
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: after mtuProbeInterval, the path MTU search runs again from 1098 to 1500
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[3.517 B334] A.1000 < B.2000: A 322719:323978(1259) ack 1 win 16384 # dropping, larger than the path MTU
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
